TFT Set 16 Simulator - Model Description
What It Is
A full-game simulator that models complete 8-player TFT lobbies from round 0 through elimination. It's ~16,400 lines of Python across two main subsystems: a game loop (simulator/game/, ~3,200 lines) and a combat engine (simulator/core/, ~13,200 lines covering hex-grid physics, abilities, items, traits).

Architecture
Game Loop (simulator/game/)

8 players each with HP, gold, level, board (4x7 hex), bench (9 slots), item bench
Shared champion pool with real depletion mechanics (buying removes copies, selling/elimination returns them)
Level-based shop odds with weighted random sampling from the remaining pool
Full economy: 5 base gold + interest (1g per 10g, max 5) + streak bonuses + passive XP
Augment selection at rounds 4, 11, 18 with tier-dependent probabilities (18 joint sequences)
Carousel rounds with HP-ordered picks
Matchmaking avoids repeat opponents, ghost army for odd player counts
Combat Engine (simulator/core/combat_engine.py - 4,679 lines)

60 Hz tick-based simulation on hex grid with A* pathfinding
Physical/Magic/True damage with armor/MR mitigation
Mana generation on damage dealt and taken (capped at 42.5)
Attack speed 0.5-5.0 hard cap, star-level scaling (2-star = 1.8x HP, 1.5x AD)
CC types: Stun, Fear (random movement), Taunt (forced target), Root (no movement)
DOT system with burn ticks, sunder/shred expiry tracking
Champion Abilities (simulator/core/champion_abilities.py - 5,124 lines)

103/106 champions have custom _cast_* handlers
Examples: Aatrox 3-hit combo with execute, Volibear 3-cast transform, Fizz untargetable jump, Jinx form-swap
Item Effects (simulator/core/item_effects.py - 1,245 lines)

6 hook types: on_hit, on_ability, on_damage_dealt, on_damage_taken, passive, combat_start
134 craftable items defined, 62 with unique effect handlers
41 artifacts - Darkin items, DFG, RFC, Silvermere, Titanic, etc.
8 Bilgewater items - burn/chill, bleed DOTs, executes
19 Piltover modules - fire at 8s with stat buffs, shields, damage, CC
22 emblem items for trait activation
Radiant items inherit base effects automatically
Traits - 53 total in traits.json, ~32 with active combat implementations

~21 with TraitManager stat buffs (Arcanist AP, Defender Armor/MR, Bruiser HP, etc.)
~9 region traits with combat bonuses (Demacia, Freljord, Void, etc.)
~13 handled in champion_abilities (Huntress, Blacksmith, etc.)
2 non-combat (Chronokeeper XP, Targon)
Combat-time logic: Warden shields, Slayer AD scaling, Gunslinger procs, Zaun shimmer, Piltover modules
AI Agents
fast_random_agent: O(1) weighted action sampling (default, optimized for speed)
econ_agent: Saves for interest, levels to 8, buys pairs
slam_agent: Equips items immediately, buys everything, levels aggressively
MixedLobbyAgent: Different strategies per player in the same game
Output
Training data: ~128 rows per game (1 per player per round) with board state, traits, economy, and final placement label
Analytics: Champion/augment/comp winrates aggregated across games
Formats: Parquet chunks (if pyarrow) or JSONL, streamed to avoid OOM
Performance
0.87s/game single core, ~2.9 games/sec on 4 workers
1M games: ~7.6 hrs on 32 cores, 14 min on 1024 cores ($19 AWS spot)
Deterministic with seed-based RNG, checkpoint/resume for long runs
Fidelity: ~85-90%
Area	Fidelity	Notes
Champion pool	95-100%	Depletion, return, weighted sampling
Economy	95-100%	Interest, streaks, XP, leveling
Combat physics	90-95%	Hex grid, A* pathfinding, damage/mana
Champion abilities	90%	103/106 handlers, some simplified
Items	85-90%	134 base + 41 artifacts + 8 Bilgewater + 19 Piltover
Traits	85-90%	53 total, ~32 with active combat logic
Augment effects	70-80%	AugmentManager applies 284 active augments via 6 categories (team stat, trait-conditional, champion-specific, hex effect, on-event, item-conditional)
PvE rounds	Low	Grants gold/items but no combat
The biggest remaining gaps are augment fidelity (284 active augments are categorized and applied, but some complex augment interactions may be simplified), some artifact items being stats-only, and missing missile speed data for 36 ranged champions.
